### Page-by-Page Redesign Plan

#### 1. [LoginPage](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/pages/auth/LoginPage.jsx#4-83) — Minor Polish
- Replace `system-ui` with design system font token
- Use `spacing` tokens instead of raw pixels
- Add keyboard `Enter` handler for form submission

#### 2. [DashboardPage](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/pages/dashboard/DashboardPage.jsx#9-73) — **Major Overhaul**
- **Row 1:** Command Center strip ([ESGScoreCard](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/components/cards/ESGScoreCard.jsx#6-34) + [TrendAreaChart](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/components/charts/TrendAreaChart.jsx#5-24) + `RiskIndicator` + cert count)
- **Row 2:** ESG Triad (3 pillar cards with sub-breakdowns)
- **Row 3:** Emissions Intelligence (enhanced [EmissionsChart](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/components/charts/EmissionsChart.jsx#3-28) with bars + intensity)
- **Row 4:** Quick Actions strip (top 3 priority actions from gap analysis)
- Wire `RiskIndicator` (currently unused) into dashboard
- Replace hardcoded `system-ui` with theme typography

#### 3. [CertificationsPage](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/pages/certifications/CertificationsPage.jsx#4-13) — **Build from Scratch**
- Header with overall readiness stat
- Grid of `CertificationDetailCard` components for IGBC, LEED, ISO 14001, NABH, GRI, BRSR, CDP, ISSB
- Selected cert detail panel with requirements checklist
- Gap severity indicators and timeline roadmap

#### 4. `AssessmentWizardPage` — Refinement
- **Step 1 (DataUpload):** Extract inline style objects to reusable style constants. No functional changes.
- **Step 2 (Summary):** Break the 149-LOC monolith into extracted sub-section components.
- **Step 3 (Results):** Replace hardcoded `strengths[]`, `gaps[]`, `roadmap[]` with computed values from scores. Break 195-LOC into sub-components.

#### 5. `ReportsPage` / `SettingsPage` — Stub Enhancement
- Add meaningful placeholder content with feature preview cards

